{"name":"Independence","hex":"#4c516d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Independence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Calaveras County, California.\nA census-designated place, the county seat of Inyo County, California.\nA ghost town in Pitkin County, Colorado.\nAn unincorporated community in Warren Township, Warren County, Indiana.\nA city, the county seat of Buchanan County, Iowa.\nA city, the county seat of Montgomery County, Kansas.\nA city in Kentucky, and one of the two county seats of Kenton County. \nA town in Tangipahoa Parish, Louisiana.\nA city in Hennepin County, Minnesota.\nAn unincorporated community in St. Louis County, Minnesota.\nA census-designated place in Tate County, Mississippi.\nA city in Missouri, United States and one of the two county seats of Jackson County.\n\nA town in Allegany County, New York.\nA river in New York; rising in Big Moose and flowing into the Black River at Pine Grove.\nA city in Cuyahoga County, Ohio.\nAn unincorporated community in Defiance County, Ohio.\nA ghost town in Custer County, Oklahoma.\nA city in Polk County, Oregon; named for the city in Missouri.\nAn unincorporated community in Henderson County, Tennessee.\nAn unincorporated community in Washington County, Texas.\nAn unincorporated community in Uintah County, Utah.\nA town in Wasatch County, Utah.\nA town, the county seat of Grayson County, Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Barbour County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Clay County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Jackson County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Preston County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Thurston County, Washington.\nA city in Trempealeau County, Wisconsin.\nA number of townships in the United States, listed under Independence Township.","An unincorporated community in Calaveras County, California."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Independence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Independence","blocks":[{"text":"Independence is a condition of a nation, country, or state, in which residents and population, or some portion thereof, exercise self-government, and usually sovereignty, over its territory. The opposite of independence is the status of a dependent territory or colony. The commemoration of the independence day of a country or nation celebrates when a country is free from all forms of colonialism; free to build a country or nation without any interference from other nations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Declaration_of_Independence_%281819%29%2C_by_John_Trumbull.jpg/330px-Declaration_of_Independence_%281819%29%2C_by_John_Trumbull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence","wikidata":"Q37055"},{"title":"Independence (probability theory)","blocks":[{"text":"Independence is a fundamental notion in probability theory, as in statistics and the theory of stochastic processes. Two events are independent, statistically independent, or stochastically independent if, informally speaking, the occurrence of one does not affect the probability of occurrence of the other or, equivalently, does not affect the odds. Similarly, two random variables are independent if the realization of one does not affect the probability distribution of the other. Conversely, dependence is when the occurrence of one event does affect the likelihood of another."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Standard_deviation_diagram_micro.svg/330px-Standard_deviation_diagram_micro.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence_(probability_theory)","wikidata":"Q625303"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/JuraIndependencia.jpg/500px-JuraIndependencia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/JuraIndependencia.jpg/500px-JuraIndependencia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Chile, one of several Spanish territories in South America, issued a Declaration of independence in 1818","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJuraIndependencia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Fran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_%281844%29.jpg/500px-Fran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_%281844%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Fran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_%281844%29.jpg/1280px-Fran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_%281844%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Fran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_%281844%29.jpg/500px-Fran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_%281844%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prince Pedro surrounded by a crowd in São Paulo after breaking the news of Brazil's independence on 7 September 1822.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFran%C3%A7ois-Ren%C3%A9_Moreaux_%E2%80%93_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Independ%C3%AAncia_(1844).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Senate1917.jpg/500px-Senate1917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum